oint you know you kind of have  to just swallow a couple of really goofy  elements when it comes to the Christmas  episodes and I think it's just a good  Doctor Who version of the classic  Christmas story of Scrooge  I think it makes its intentions clear  upfront it does it very well there's  some really heartfelt moments in it I  enjoy it number four  last Christmas if it wasn't for one  specific thing about this this might  even be my number one but I'll come back  to that so this one should be tonal  whiplash because we literally have Santa  Claus yet at the same time have  something that looks like the face  hugger from alien doing this dream  within a dream waking nightmare thing  these two things should not go together  and I wouldn't be shocked to find out in  the comments at the end of all this that  for some people they don't go together  but for me somehow yeah it works I mean  a big part of it is Nick Frost is  wonderful as Santa he's got a terrific  chemistry bouncing off of Capaldi and  then for some reason like how dark and  cerebral the story gets really works for  me it's hard for me to nail down exactly  why that is now the one thing that I'll  say that drags this thing down is that  this marks the second of what would  ultimately end up being three perfectly  good exit points for Clara to leave the  show but then she doesn't there was one  in death in heaven they'd be one later  and face the Raven and there's this one  here and each time finding out she was  coming back after that perfectly good  exit always frustrated me and in this  one they actually have her comeback in  the episode itself and it's annoying  because she was good in the episode and  it would have been a perfectly good  satisfying leap off point for her and  they didn't do it so that ends up being  a somewhat hefty black mark on an  episode that I otherwise really liked  number three the husbands of River Song  so this one it's interesting that  oftentimes with these ones that end